## Requirements

- Node.js **>= 22.18.0** (the `engines` field is enforced by npm).
- **Zero runtime dependencies.** `dependencies` is empty and stays empty unless you change
  it deliberately.
- Two dev-only tools, needed to compile and test: `typescript` and `@types/node`
  (`devDependencies`). They are never installed for consumers of the published package.

```sh
npm install             # installs the dev toolchain
npm install --omit=dev  # if you only want to run the CLI
```

## Install

```sh
npm install          # installs the dev toolchain; there are no runtime dependencies
pnpm add -g .        # global install with pnpm
npx .                # run straight from the folder
```

## Usage

```sh
{{CLI_BIN}} --help
{{CLI_BIN}} --version
{{CLI_BIN}} hash "hello"      # -> sha256 hex digest
{{CLI_BIN}} slug "Hello World" # -> hello-world
{{CLI_BIN}} selftest          # built-in checks, exits 0 when they pass
```

Run the CLI straight from a checkout, with no install and no build step:

```sh
node bin/{{CLI_BIN}}.mjs hash "hello"
node bin/{{CLI_BIN}}.mjs slug "Hello World"
```

The CLI loads the built `dist/index.js` when it is present and falls back to `src/index.ts`
otherwise, which Node >= 22.18 loads natively by stripping the types. So every subcommand
works on a fresh clone, before `npm install` and before `npm run build`.

### Library

```ts
import { sha256, slugify } from '{{PACKAGE_NAME}}';

sha256('abc');           // 'ba7816bf8f01cfea414140de5dae2223b00361a396177a9cb410ff61f20015ad'
slugify('The Long Song') // 'the-long-song'
```

The entry point is the built output, so `npm run build` must succeed before
`npm pack` or `npm publish`. Consumers see `dist/index.js` plus `dist/index.d.ts`.

## Scripts

| Script | What it does |
| --- | --- |
| `npm run build` | Compile `src/` to `dist/` with type declarations. |
| `npm run typecheck` | Type-check without emitting. |
| `npm run lint` | Type-check, then syntax-check the `bin/` entry. No style rules. |
| `npm test` | Build, then run the `node:test` suite over `dist/**/*.test.js`. |
| `npm run selftest` | Run the CLI's own built-in checks. Needs no build. |
| `npm run clean` | Delete `dist/`. |

`lint` is deliberately weak: this package has no linter dependency, so it runs the two
checks Node and `tsc` can do for free. It will not catch style, unused exports or
suspicious patterns. Add ESLint, Biome or whatever your team uses, and wire it into this
script, once you decide that is worth the dependencies.

The glob in `npm test` is deliberate. `node --test dist/` reports success while running
nothing at all, and a bare `node --test` in the project root picks up `src/index.test.ts`,
which cannot resolve its `./index.js` import before a build. Test the compiled output
explicitly.

## Publishing notes

- `publishConfig.access` is `public`.
- `repository` is **not** set. This scaffold cannot know where the code lives, and it will
  not invent a URL. Add `repository`, `homepage` and `bugs` before publishing.
- `npm pack` ships `bin/`, `dist/`, `README.md` and `LICENSE` only. Run the build first;
  a stale `dist/` is published as-is.
- Because `files` includes all of `dist/`, the compiled `index.test.js` ships too. Harmless,
  and no dev dependency is needed to run it. If you would rather not publish it, list the
  `dist/` files you want explicitly in `files` instead of the whole directory.
- `.npmignore` cannot trim anything `files` already asked for. It is there as a fallback.
- The `bin` **file name** is fixed at `bin/melodie-app.mjs`. The `bin` **key** in
  `package.json` is templated, so if you renamed the key, rename the file to match or the
  installed command will not resolve.

## Security

- No network access, no environment variables, no child processes.
- The only filesystem reads are the CLI's own `dist/index.js` or `src/index.ts`. Both are
  local files inside the package.
- No wallet, key, token or transaction handling of any kind.
- Keep it that way unless you have a reason and a reviewer.

